# Low-index four-group conjugation in the native Mathieu 22 Sylow

Eight explicit conjugates rule out each involution outside twelve certified
rows when its centralizer index is at most six. The remaining commuting pairs
continue to commute after conjugation by every row of the full automorphism
Sylow subgroup. These are checked permutation identities for the actual
source32 Mathieu-cover screen, not assumptions about an abstract catalogue.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, the local inspection preceding 2.4.32, p.547.
-/

